  "id": "COMPOUND:31981 - PROTEIN:6058",
  "verbalization": "Albiflorin is implicated in the biological pathway leading to the Myelin transcription factor 1 through multiple indirect mechanisms. The evidence suggests that Albiflorin acts as a target of several compounds, including (2S)-2-Methyl-1-[1,3,7,9-Tetrahydroxy-2,8-Dimethyl-6-(2-Methylpropanoyl)Dibenzofuran-4-Yl]Butan-1-One, 6,7-Dimethyl-8-ribityllumazine, and 24-Propylidenecholesta-5,25-dien-3beta-ol, all of which are known to target the Myelin transcription factor 1. These compounds are likely involved in the regulation of myelin-related processes, and their interaction with Albiflorin may contribute to the activation or modulation of the Myelin transcription factor 1. The integrated evidence suggests a potential role for Albiflorin in the regulation of myelin transcription factors, possibly through the activation of downstream signaling pathways. The relationship is supported by the shared target of multiple compounds, indicating a possible functional link between Albiflorin and the Myelin transcription factor 1.",
